    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Colleran Auctioneer`s is pleased to present this substantial four-bedroom detached dormer positioned on a highly coveted, elevated site along Kingston Road, Galway. Scaraveen`, Kingston Road, Galway offers uninterrupted stunning views across Galway Golf Club and Galway Bay. While it boasts an exceptional architectural footprint and a premium location, this home now requires modernisation and renovation throughout. This property is being sold as a blank canvas, offering an incredible opportunity for a buyer to recreate a bespoke, energy-efficient dream home tailored to their own taste.\n\nThe ground floor layout is exceptionally generous in scale, providing a strong structural foundation for a modern re-design. An entrance porch leads to an entrance hall featuring a traditional quarter-turn staircase. To the left, a dual-aspect sitting room with floor-to-ceiling windows offers a grand scale formal room with French doors leading to the dining room. To the right, a separate, secondary living room with double floor-to-ceiling front windows overlooks the mature front garden. To the rear of the ground floor, a spacious kitchen featuring a distinct bay window overlooks the beautiful back garden, while a utility room and an adjacent guest WC offer extra facilities. A highly functional semi-integrated side hall that gives sheltered external access to a boiler house and a dedicated laundry/wet room will be ideal as a future mudroom space.\n\nUpstairs, the turning staircase splits into a walk-in hot press on one side and a bright, spacious landing on the other, and is flooded by natural light from twin dormer windows. An expansive main bedroom suite has a walk-in dressing room, an ensuite bathroom and fabulous panoramic views of the Galway Golf Course, Galway Bay and the Clare hills. The three additional double bedrooms are all equally well sized and clustered around a centrally located, spacious family bathroom.\n\nOutside, the site features mature, landscaped front and rear gardens bordered by large evergreen hedges that offer excellent privacy. A natural stone boundary wall defines the front entrance, which opens to a wide tarmac driveway providing ample off-street parking,\n\nThis property is an ideal prospect for forward-thinking families looking to acquire a high-profile site, with amazing views in one of Galway`s premier locations. The below video gives an indication of the development potential for this site, subject to planning permission. Guiding at 850,000, early viewing is strongly recommended. \n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Porch - 2.9m (9'6\") x 2.1m (6'11\")\nWith tiled floor.\n\nEntrance Hall - 4.5m (14'9\") x 3m (9'10\")\nWith built in closet and quarter turn staircase to spacious first floor landing.\n\nSitting Room - 8.4m (27'7\") x 4.5m (14'9\")\nWith coving to ceiling, feature marble fireplace and dual aspect floor to ceiling windows. French doors lead to dining room.\n\nDining Room - 4.4m (14'5\") x 3m (9'10\")\nWith coving to ceiling and picture window overlooking the back garden.\n\nLiving Room - 4.6m (15'1\") x 4.2m (13'9\")\nWith open fireplace and two floor to ceiling windows overlooking the front garden.\n\nKitchen - 7.3m (23'11\") x 3.1m (10'2\")\nWith built in and overhead kitchen units and a bay window overlooking the mature and landscaped back garden.\n\nUtility Room - 3m (9'10\") x 2.5m (8'2\")\nWith sink unit, overhead units and plumbed for washing machine.\n\nGuest WC - 2.2m (7'3\") x 1m (3'3\")\nWith toilet and wash hand basin.\n\nFirst Floor\n\nLanding - 4.4m (14'5\") x 2.7m (8'10\")\nThe staircase turns at the top, leading to the hot press on one side and a spacious, bright landing on the other, featuring two dormer windows.\n\nMain Bedroom - 5.6m (18'4\") x 4.6m (15'1\")\nWith a six-door built-in wardrobe and walk-in dressing room (2.0m x 1.6m), enjoying views over Galway Golf Course and beyond to Galway Bay.\n\nEnsuite - 3.2m (10'6\") x 1.6m (5'3\")\nWith toilet, shower and wash hand basin.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.7m (12'2\") x 2.8m (9'2\")\n\nBedroom 3 - 4.5m (14'9\") x 3.9m (12'10\")\nWith built in wardrobe and vanity unit.\n\nBedroom 4 - 4.5m (14'9\") x 3.7m (12'2\")\nWith built in wardrobe and vanity unit.\n\nBathroom - 3.3m (10'10\") x 2.5m (8'2\")\nWith bath, toilet and wash hand basin.\n\nArea\nThis house is approximately 258 sqm / 2,777 sq.ft.\n\nGardens\nThe mature front garden is landscaped, lawned and bordered on both sides by large evergreen hedging. A stone wall defines the front boundary, while a tarmac driveway provides ample off-street parking. The rear garden is also landscaped with mature shrubs and enclosed by evergreen hedging, offering excellent privacy. A patio provides space for outdoor dining, and a timber garden shed offers useful outdoor storage.\n\nExternal Rooms\nA semi-integrated hall, open to the front of the property, leads to the boiler house and laundry/wet room (3.0m x 1.5m). This space also provides sheltered access to the side and rear of the house, making it a practical entrance for families returning from outdoor sports or activities.\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
